{# Squelette = page-level layout.

   Two named blocks, and the renderer renders them OUT OF ORDER: `body` first, then `head`
   (ticket 15, ADR-0014). That is what lets <head> carry every asset the page turned out to
   need -- by the time it renders, every action, field and included page has declared its own.
   Before this, assets registered during the page body could only be flushed at </body>,
   stylesheets included, so content was painted before its own styles arrived.

   Consequences for a theme author:
     - `{{ page_content|raw }}` is where the page goes. The old `{WIKINI_PAGE}` brace marker
       was plain text the renderer split the file on; it no longer exists.
     - `{{ declared_assets() }}` goes LAST in the head block. It emits everything declared, and
       an action written after it in that block would register too late to be included.
     - `{{linkstyle}}` and `{{linkjavascript}}` are gone. Nothing replaces them: assets are
       declared by whatever needs them and emitted once, here.
     - Actions may still be called anywhere in either block -- that freedom is why this is two
       Twig blocks rather than a fixed set of pre-rendered slots.

   Ticket 16 (internal navigation loads through htmx) adds four more, all inside the body
   block, because the body block is exactly what a boosted navigation swaps:
     - `hx-boost` on <body>, behind the `htmx_navigation` config flag, plus `hx-headers`
       carrying the layout fingerprint. That is what lets the server notice that the page you
       are going to uses a different squelette/theme/lang and answer with a real navigation
       instead of swapping its body into the wrong chrome.
     - `{{ page_state() }}` FIRST inside the block: the `wiki` globals and any flash message.
       Inline markup further down calls `_t()`, which reads `wiki.lang`.
     - a `.yw-progress` element for `hx-indicator` -- an XHR navigation shows no browser
       progress, so without it a slow page looks like a dead click.
     - `#yw-main` focusable (`tabindex="-1"`) and a polite live region, so a swap moves
       keyboard focus and is announced instead of silently replacing the page. #}
{% block head %}
<!doctype html>
{# `--yw-navbar-height` rides on the root element rather than in a stylesheet, and
   deliberately: an inline custom property beats the same property declared in ANY
   stylesheet -- preset, theme or custom.css -- with no `!important` anywhere. That is
   what "the Layout screen has the last word" means (ticket 30). #}
<html lang="{{ action('configuration param="lang"') }}" style="{{ layout_root_style() }}">
<head>
  <!-- HTML Metas -->
  <meta charset="{{ action('configuration param="charset"') }}">
  {{ action('metarobots')|raw }}
  <meta name="keywords" content="{{ action('configuration param="meta_keywords"') }}" />
  <meta name="description" content="{{ action('configuration param="meta_description"') }}" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />

  <!-- Title of the page -->
  <title>{{ action('configuration param="wakka_name"') }} : {{ action('pagetitle')|raw }}</title>

  {{ action('favicon')|raw }}
  {{ action('linkrss')|raw }}

  {# every stylesheet and script the whole page declared -- keep this last #}
  {{ declared_assets()|raw }}
</head>
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<body {{ action('parambody')|raw }}{% if htmx_navigation %} hx-boost="true" hx-indicator=".yw-progress" hx-headers='{"{{ layout_fingerprint_header }}": "{{ layout_fingerprint }}"}'{% endif %}>
  {{ page_state()|raw }}

  {# htmx-indicator: hidden until a request is in flight; the CSS delays it so a fast
     navigation shows nothing at all rather than a flicker #}
  <div class="yw-progress htmx-indicator" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  {# what assistive technology is told after a swap; yw-navigation.js writes the page title
     here. Empty and polite: it must announce the arrival, not narrate the page. #}
  <div id="yw-navigation-announcer" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>

  <div id="yw-container">

    <a id="yw-a11y-jump-content" class="sr-only sr-only-focusable yw-btn" href="#yw-main">
      Aller au contenu principal
    </a>

    {# Ticket 30: the brand, the navbar and the quick menu come from `layout_*` configuration,
       edited on /admin/layout. They were three wiki pages (`PageTitre`, `PageMenuHaut`,
       `PageRapideHaut`) included here and re-parsed on every render.
       The banner, the side menu and the footer are still pages, and still `{{include}}`d:
       what people put in them is arbitrary wiki content, which is what a page is for.
       `layout_page()` rather than the name itself, because a page may name a different
       banner or footer for itself -- the per-page override, which survives for these three. #}
    {# `id="yw-layout-chrome"` is load-bearing: the live preview on /admin/layout swaps this
       block's contents for the same fragment rendered from the form being filled in. #}
    <nav id="yw-topnav" class="fixable" role="navigation">
      <div class="container" id="yw-layout-chrome">
        {{ layout_chrome()|raw }}
      </div>
    </nav>

    {# The banner and the footer are pages, and the pencil beside each opens that page --
       for whoever may write it. `layout_edit()` answers '' for everyone else. #}
    <header id="yw-header" class="yw-chrome-editable">
      {{ layout_edit('header')|raw }}
      {{ action('include page="' ~ layout_page('PageHeader') ~ '" class="yw-headerpage" doubleclick="1"')|raw }}
    </header>

    <div id="yw-main" role="main" tabindex="-1" {{ action('doubleclick')|raw }}>
      <div class="yw-main-content alone">
        {{ page_content|raw }}
      </div>
      {# inside #yw-main, which is what gives the page its column: the line of facts the
         edit bar ends with is a footnote to the page and lines up with it. (The cluster of
         actions is `position: fixed`, so where it sits in the markup changes nothing about
         where it lands.) #}
      {{ action('editbar')|raw }}
    </div>

    <footer id="yw-footer">
      <div class="container yw-chrome-editable">
        {{ layout_edit('footer')|raw }}
        {{ action('include page="' ~ layout_page('PageFooter') ~ '" class="footerpage" doubleclick="1"')|raw }}
      </div> <!-- /.container -->
    </footer><!-- /#yw-footer -->
  </div> <!-- /#yw-container -->

</body>
</html>
{% endblock %}
